# /sdlc-setup

Run `./scripts/sdlc setup` (on Windows PowerShell or cmd: `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd setup`). It installs the dependencies of every part of the project.
The first run downloads packages and can take minutes: give the command up to 10 minutes (or run it in the background and wait for it).

- It succeeds: say what it installed and suggest `/sdlc-verify` next.
- It fails: show which step failed and the log it names under `.ai/evidence/`, and say what the log says. Do not retry blindly, and do not edit a dependency
  manifest or a lockfile to make it pass. If a tool is missing, run `./scripts/sdlc doctor` and show what it reports.
- It stops because a person has to decide something (for example it offers to install Python): pass the question on word for word and stop.
- Never use `sudo` or an administrator shell.
